    "note": "Read is the 2nd Substitute (Gray) as amended by House committee 2-14-2024, not the enrolled version; later amendments are not in the text read. The lead-in to subsection (2) (agency reports 'Beginning on July 1, 2026 ... annually on or before April 30' to the commission, excluding the Department of Corrections) is garbled by stray marks in the print, so it is not quoted; item (a), the number of firearms seized from restricted persons, is split by a page break and is also omitted. Other sections renumber and restructure Title 53 reporting provisions, not a separate gun-unrelated policy topic."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 7 (new Utah Code 53-25-501): (c) \"Restricted person\" means a Category I or Category II restricted person as defined in Section 76-10-503.\nSection 7 (new Utah Code 53-25-501): (b) the types of firearms the law enforcement agency lawfully seized from restricted persons; (c) information on where the restricted persons obtained the firearms seized by the law enforcement agency if the information is known or discoverable by the law enforcement agency; and (d) the reasons under Subsection 76-10-503(1)(a) or (b) that made the individuals who had weapons seized restricted persons."
}